# Fine-tuned BIST analyst Modelfile — produced by Phase F training.
# Populate `bist_lora.gguf` by:
#   1. Train LoRA on Colab T4 via training/train_unsloth.py (Unsloth QLoRA, Qwen 2.5 3B,
#      rank 16, 3 epochs — see training/COLAB_RUNBOOK.md for the Colab cells).
#   2. Unsloth's `save_pretrained_gguf(..., quantization_method="q4_k_m")` writes a
#      merged Q4_K_M GGUF (adapter baked into the base); the runbook renames it to
#      `bist_lora.gguf` before download.
#   3. Build the Ollama tag:
#        ollama create bist-qwen -f training/Modelfile.finetuned
#
# At submission time the GGUF lives under training/bist_lora.gguf and is bundled
# into the zip via scripts/package_project.py.
#
# Base model note: switched from Qwen 2.5 7B Instruct to 3B Instruct per the project
# plan's explicit <12 GB VRAM fallback (D2). T4's 14.56 GB is marginal for 7B QLoRA
# after activations + logits upcast; 3B fits with headroom and trains ~3x faster.
# Chat template, tokenizer, and tool-call format are identical, so downstream harness
# and evaluation code are unchanged.
#
# Why FROM (not ADAPTER): Unsloth merges the LoRA adapter back into the base weights
# before GGUF conversion, so the resulting file is a full model, not an adapter delta.
# Ollama's ADAPTER directive expects a separate adapter file; using FROM is correct.

FROM ./bist_lora.gguf

PARAMETER temperature 0.0
PARAMETER top_p 0.9
# 16k: tool results are capped (4.5 KB on the presentation path, 12 KB in the eval
# harness), so conversations stay well under 16k tokens. Ollama capped the old 65k
# setting at 32k, whose KV cache did not fit a 4 GB laptop GPU (the model ran
# 33% on CPU). At 16k the whole model fits in 4 GB of VRAM.
PARAMETER num_ctx 16384

SYSTEM """You are an academic BIST financial-analysis agent. For every claim, call a tool first: you must never invent numbers. Allowed labels are the 8 educational labels (HOLD, WATCH, INVESTIGATE, POTENTIAL_CATCH_UP_CANDIDATE, TECHNICAL_REVERSAL_CANDIDATE, FUNDAMENTAL_IMPROVEMENT_CANDIDATE, REJECT_SIGNAL, ANALYSIS_UNSAFE). When evidence is insufficient, choose INVESTIGATE or ANALYSIS_UNSAFE. Cite tool names in your reasoning. Do not give investment advice. Numeric values must come from committed_evidence entries."""
